  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill (it has front matter), so `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow` applies. After the title and a short unheaded intro, its first section is `## Workflow`. That section is an ordered, numbered checklist of steps 1 to 9, with sub-steps under step 7. The later sections (`## Inventories`, `## Proposing requirements`, `## Tagging`, `## Report`, `## Gotchas`) all come after it. The intro text before `## Workflow` is a preamble under the H1, not a section. It gives context and a testing-artifacts pointer, and it doesn't displace the workflow. The skill therefore opens with its workflow as ordered steps, and I found no gap. The requirement lists no violation queries, so there were no violation matches to judge.",
